# LD-040 UAT latency SMOKE SAMPLE, 2026-10-24 (UTC 18:23-18:25). NOT a load test.
# Target https://lawdesk.167-86-90-174.sslip.io, read-only QA account qa.viewer (role QA_READ_ONLY: CASE_VIEW,
# COURT_VIEW, JUDGMENT_VIEW, PROCEEDING_VIEW), credential file read in-process by deploy/qa/qa_accounts.py Session,
# never printed. Sequential, at most 1 request per second. Requests sent to UAT in total: 60 (limit 60):
#   1  curl GET /actuator/health (reachability check)                            -> 200 in 206 ms
#   54 run 1 (csrf, sign-in, 51 GETs, sign-out)
#   5  run 2 (csrf, sign-in, 2 GETs, sign-out; csrf did not need a refresh before sign-out)
# No body, cookie or token is recorded here.

## Run 1: INVALID latency figures (instrumentation defect, kept for transparency)
# The timer wrapped the pacing wait as well as the HTTP exchange, so every figure is ~1 s (the pacing interval).
# Statuses are valid: 50/50 reads answered 200.
